BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Limey (1999)
DTSTART:20251030T023000Z
DTEND:20251030T042000Z
DTSTAMP:20251030T023000Z
UID:pxSlhr1Oxe
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nL.A. Noir: Shadows in Paradise Pr
 esented by Greg Olson Productions In the period between director Steven So
 derbergh’s stunning indy Cannes debut sex\, lies and videotape (1991) an
 d his mainstream 2000s triumphs like Erin Brockovich\, Traffic\, and Ocean
 ’s Eleven\, he crafted this lean\, compelling quest film with a counterc
 ulture vibe. Aging Cockney ex-con Wilson (Swinging Sixties British icon Te
 rence Stamp) flies into L.A. when he learns his dear daughter Jenny (Melis
 sa George) died in a car crash. Her death was suspicious\, and Wilson take
 s it upon himself to get answers. The road leads to Valentine (icon of Hip
  Peter Fonda) music world mogul and drug trafficker\, who was Jenny’s la
 st boyfriend. Valentine’s surrounded by protectors (Barry Newman of the 
 1971 cult favorite Vanishing Point)\, but Wilson gets help from Jenny’s 
 friends (Luis Guzman\, cult Cool Girl Leslie Ann Warren). Wilson’s bent 
 on cold\, icy revenge\, but director Soderbergh calls the tune. With Warho
 l star Joe Dellesandro\, George Clooney (uncredited archive footage). Indi
 vidual Tickets: $15Passes: Prorated\, with discounts for SIFF\, SAM\, Swed
 ish Club\, UW Cinema Studies\, NWFF\, SFI\, TheFilmSchool\, Festa Italiana
 \, Alliance Francaise de Seattle\, Scarecrow Video\, & KING FM members\n\n
 https://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/la-noir-shadows-in-paradise/the-li
 mey
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cinema Dissection: Inglourious Basterds
DTSTART:20251101T170000Z
DTEND:20251101T232000Z
DTSTAMP:20251101T170000Z
UID:7C1b3o2jSH
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 360 mins (6h00m)\n\nFilm Talks In dark uncertain tim
 es\, the power to reimagine history becomes a revolutionary act. With Ingl
 ourious Basterds\, Quentin Tarantino fuses revenge fantasy with metafictio
 n\, asking us to reflect not just on history\, but on how it’s told. In 
 this Cinema Dissection\, local filmmaker and PBS producer Jeremy Cropf lea
 ds a detailed\, shot-by-shot analysis of how the film’s formal elements
 —long takes\, stylized violence\, genre blending\, and tonal shifts—re
 veal deeper truths about who controls the stories we inherit. From the ico
 nic opening to the blazing finale\, join us as we explore the film's layer
 ed commentary on mythmaking\, propaganda\, and cultural memory.\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/programs-and-events/education/adult-film-education/film-talk
 s/cinema-dissection-inglourious-basterds
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ascent (1977)
DTSTART:20251106T020000Z
DTEND:20251106T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20251106T020000Z
UID:nZf50CJ5pm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club Shepitko’s emo
 tionally overwhelming final film won the Golden Bear at the 1977 Berlin Fi
 lm Festival and has been hailed around the world as the finest Soviet film
  of its decade. Set during World War II's darkest days\, The Ascent follow
 s the path of two peasant soldiers\, cut off from their troop\, who trudge
  through the snowy backwoods of Belarus seeking refuge among villagers. Th
 eir harrowing trek leads them on a journey of betrayal\, heroism\, and ult
 imate transcendence.  Introduced by SIFF Cinema Staff Member Adam Plesser
 .\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-club/the-ascent
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drive (2011)
DTSTART:20251106T033000Z
DTEND:20251106T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20251106T033000Z
UID:fuHZP1nsDA
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nL.A. Noir: Shadows in Paradise P
 resented by Greg Olson Productions Driver (Ryan Gosling) travels light. Je
 ans\, T-shirt\, jacket’s got a scorpion design. He’s an ace at the whe
 el\, for money he’ll drive for you whether your purpose is light (he’s
  a Hollywood stunt driver) or dark (criminal activities). Driver’s preci
 se\, in control\, so when he says he’ll do his job for you\, takes your 
 payment for working exactly so many minutes and seconds\, that’s all you
  get. Self-contained\, tiny apartment. When he shares an elevator ride wit
 h a sweet-looking woman (Carey Mulligan) they just exchange a shy\, split-
 second glance\, no words. But there’s an unstated hum of connection betw
 een them that persists after her husband (Oscar Issac) comes home from pri
 son. Gosling personifies the Romantic Movement\, like a troubadour of old 
 pledged to his lady in spirit. There are good guys (Breaking Bad’s Bryan
  Cranston) and bad guys (Albert Brooks\, Ron Perlman\, Mad Men’s Christi
 na Hendricks) to complicate things\, but Gosling will drive Mulligan in th
 e golden afternoon and through the night\, have no fear. Individual Ticket
 s: $15Passes: Prorated\, with discounts for SIFF\, SAM\, Swedish Club\, UW
  Cinema Studies\, NWFF\, SFI\, TheFilmSchool\, Festa Italiana\, Alliance F
 rancaise de Seattle\, Scarecrow Video\, & KING FM members\n\nhttps://www.s
 iff.net/cinema/in-theaters/la-noir-shadows-in-paradise/drive
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Inherent Vice (2014)
DTSTART:20251113T033000Z
DTEND:20251113T062000Z
DTSTAMP:20251113T033000Z
UID:i39x7qBMKk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 148 mins (2h28m)\n\nL.A. Noir: Shadows in Paradise P
 resented by Greg Olson Productions Always in the vanguard\, New/Old Hollyw
 ood director Paul Thomas Anderson made The Phantom Thread (2017) in Englan
 d\, but otherwise his personal and cinematic turf has been Los Angeles and
  its environs in Hard Eight\, Boogie Nights\, Magnolia\, Punch-Drunk Love\
 , There Will Be Blood\, The Master\, Licorice Pizza. And here we have the 
 Gordita Beach town of Thomas Pynchon’s delightfully dense Inherent Vice 
 novel. Pynchon and Anderson waft us back to the late 1960s-early 1970s lik
 e no one else can: ride the vibes. Smoking a joint helps charmingly semi-f
 ocused detective Doc Sportello (a transcendent Joaquin Phoenix) see all th
 e dimensions of a case. Of course Doc’s office is in a medical clinic\; 
 we’re in Pynchon’s brilliant\, satirical universe here\, where beauty\
 , menace\, absurdity\, heart and soul mix it up minute to minute. One nigh
 t Doc’s former girlfriend Shasta (Katherine Waterston) comes to him. Whe
 re’s she been\, why’s she afraid\, where did she go in that big black 
 Cadillac? As Doc embarks on a steps-forward/steps-backward quest to solve 
 her mysteries\, he encounters the sinister Golden Fang organization\, a pr
 esumed-dead sax player (Owen Wilson)\, a trippy carnival of SoCal human wi
 ldlife\, and his nemesis/friend/sparring partner policeman Bigfoot (a stel
 lar James Brolin). Doc’s counterculture values and ways are mocked and a
 ttacked\, but he rides them like a heartfelt wave. Features a glorious pas
 sage of Neil Young’s music. With Reese Witherspoon\, Martin Short\, Beni
 cio del Toro. Individual Tickets: $15Passes: Prorated\, with discounts for
  SIFF\, SAM\, Swedish Club\, UW Cinema Studies\, NWFF\, SFI\, TheFilmSchoo
 l\, Festa Italiana\, Alliance Francaise de Seattle\, Scarecrow Video\, & K
 ING FM members\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/la-noir-shadows-
 in-paradise/inherent-vice
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
